    {
      "text": "he that endureth to the end, Matt. 10:22 (24:13; Mark 13:13). have no root … and so endure but for a time, Mark 4:17. that meat which endureth unto everlasting life, John 6:27. hopeth all things, endureth all things, 1 Cor. 13:7. I endure all things for the elect’s sakes, 2 Tim. 2:10. they will not endure sound doctrine, 2 Tim. 4:3. endure afflictions, 2 Tim. 4:5. after he had patiently endured, Heb. 6:15. in heaven a better and an enduring substance, Heb. 10:34. he endured, as seeing him who is invisible, Heb. 11:27. endured the cross, Heb. 12:2. If ye endure chastening, Heb. 12:7. Blessed is the man that endureth temptation, James 1:12. we count them happy which endure, James 5:11. But the word of the Lord endureth for ever, 1 Pet. 1:25.",
